title: The KAG in the Districts
subtitle: Levi's group is courting a district of the party.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 10 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and kag_exists = 1 and levi_in_party = 0 and e21_kagd_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 6
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_kagd_done = 1;
Q.e21_kag_outcome = 0;
var d = RG.target('loyalty');
Q.e21_kag_target = d;
Q.e21_kag_target_name = Q.sys_target_name;
Q.e21_kag_target_faction_name = Q.sys_target_faction_name;
!}

= The KAG in the Districts

The Communist Working Group has a paper and a Reichstag group, and no districts. This autumn Däumig and Malzahn have been touring [+ e21_kag_target_name +], where the leadership follows the [+ e21_kag_target_faction_name +] and trusts the Zentrale less than any other district does.

They do not attack the party at their meetings. They say they want nothing from Moscow but to be left to judge German questions for themselves. Several branch secretaries have been seen in the hall.

- @organisers: Send our best organisers to the district.
- @purge: Expel everyone who went to their meetings.
- @ignore: Leave them to it.

@organisers
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The branches are won back one by one.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money to send anyone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e21_kag_outcome = 1;
RG.district(Q.e21_kag_target, {loyalty: 10, members: -0.02});
!}

Two organisers from the Zentrale move into [+ e21_kag_target_name +] for a month and visit every branch. A few go over to the KAG anyway. Most stay, and some of them are flattered to have been asked.

@purge
subtitle: A smaller district, and of one mind. The KAG will print the names.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_kag_outcome = 2;
RG.district(Q.e21_kag_target, {members: -0.1, loyalty: 4});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The district control commission expels every member who was seen at a KAG meeting, and several who were not. The KAG's paper prints their names under the heading "Expelled for listening".

@ignore
subtitle: Costs nothing now.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_kag_outcome = 4;
RG.district(Q.e21_kag_target, {members: -0.1, loyalty: -8});
RG.news('KAG wins over party branches in ' + Q.e21_kag_target_name, 2);
!}

By December a dozen branches in [+ e21_kag_target_name +] have gone over to the KAG, with their funds and their membership lists.
